## Addendum A — LMIC Public-Sector Deployment

This addendum is incorporated into the Data Use Agreement above
when the dataset's host has marked the data as available
royalty-free for deployment in **low- and middle-income country
(LMIC) public-sector health systems** per the WHO Health Data
Governance Principles and the host's commercial-use terms.

## A.1. Scope of LMIC carve-out

The royalty waiver applies to model deployment where the operator
is:

- a national or sub-national public health authority of an LMIC as
  classified by the World Bank for the calendar year in which the
  agreement is effective; **or**
- a WHO-recognised humanitarian organisation operating in such a
  jurisdiction; **or**
- an academic institution providing clinical decision support to
  the institutions named above on a not-for-profit basis.

## A.2. Public-good obligations

In return for the royalty waiver the requester agrees:

1. To publish the model card, performance characteristics, and
   intended-use statement in an open repository under a license no
   more restrictive than CC-BY-4.0.
2. To make the model deployable on the operator's existing
   infrastructure where reasonable, including offering an on-prem
   or air-gapped deployment mode when the operator's connectivity
   constraints require it.
3. To not pursue jurisdictional protections (regulatory exclusivity
   or patent claims) that would prevent local maintenance or
   adaptation of the model by the operator's clinical or technical
   staff.

## A.3. Reporting

The requester will report annually to the host on the LMIC
deployment footprint: the operating jurisdictions, the approximate
patient population covered, and any adverse events that the
operator has surfaced. The report is summary in nature and does
not require disclosure of operator-internal data.

## A.4. Termination of the addendum

The addendum survives termination of the main agreement to the
extent of any active LMIC deployment. It may be terminated only
by mutual written consent or upon the operator ceasing operation.
